{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-001", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 1, "quote_original": "You do not command things to appear by your words or loud affirmations. Such vain repetition is more often than not confirmation of the opposite. Decreeing is ever done in consciousness.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["ASSUMPTION"], "tags": ["decreeing", "consciousness", "affirmations"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-002", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 6, "quote_original": "The awareness of being is the door through which the manifestations of life pass into the world of form.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["awareness-of-being", "door", "manifestation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-003", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 7, "quote_original": "Consciousness is the resurrecting power – resurrecting that which man is conscious of being. Man is ever out-picturing that which he is conscious of being. This is the truth that makes man free, for man is always self-imprisoned or self-freed.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT", "REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["consciousness", "self-concept", "freedom"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-004", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 12, "quote_original": "For your conviction of yourself – your opinion of yourself will determine your expression in life.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["self-concept", "conviction", "expression"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-005", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 17, "quote_original": "The signs always follow. They never precede.", "primary_topic": "ASSUMPTION", "secondary_topics": ["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["signs-follow", "order", "manifestation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-006", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 25, "quote_original": "All of your present beliefs, fears and limitations are weights that bind you to your present level of consciousness. If you would transcend this level you must leave behind all that is now your present self, or conception of yourself.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["FEAR_DOUBT", "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"], "tags": ["beliefs", "limitations", "self-concept", "transformation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-007", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 28, "quote_original": "The only way to change your expressions of life is to change your consciousness.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES", "SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["change", "consciousness", "expression"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-008", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 29, "quote_original": "In other words, you can only be to others what you are first to yourself.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["RELATIONSHIPS"], "tags": ["self-concept", "relationships", "self-perception"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-009", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 35, "quote_original": "You are one with your present conception of yourself. But you are greater than that which you are at present aware of being.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"], "tags": ["self-concept", "identity", "potential"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-010", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 39, "quote_original": "Do not speculate as to the HOW of this consciousness embodying itself, for no man is wise enough to know the how. Speculation is proof that you have not attained to the naturalness of being the thing desired and so are filled with doubts.", "primary_topic": "ASSUMPTION", "secondary_topics": ["FEAR_DOUBT", "DESIRE"], "tags": ["naturalness", "how", "doubt", "assumption"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-011", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 41, "quote_original": "When you come into the joy of thanksgiving so that you actually feel grateful for having received that which is not yet apparent to the senses, you have definitely become one in consciousness with the thing for which you gave thanks.", "primary_topic": "FEELING", "secondary_topics": ["ASSUMPTION", "FAITH_PRAYER"], "tags": ["gratitude", "thanksgiving", "wish-fulfilled"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-012", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 48, "quote_original": "Therefore, a very good practice before you enter into your meditation is first to free every man in the world from blame.", "primary_topic": "FAITH_PRAYER", "secondary_topics": ["RELATIONSHIPS"], "tags": ["meditation", "forgiveness", "blame"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-013", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 54, "quote_original": "You are at this moment calling out of the infinite that which you are now conscious of being. And not one word or conviction will fail to find you.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT", "REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["conviction", "conscious-of-being", "infinite"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-014", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 65, "quote_original": "All things must begin and end in consciousness.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["consciousness", "cause", "reality"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-015", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 75, "quote_original": "Stop asking yourself whether you are worthy or unworthy to receive that which you desire.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["worthiness", "desire", "self-worth"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-016", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 76, "quote_original": "Your desires contain within themselves the plan of self-expression.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["desire", "self-expression", "plan"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-017", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 78, "quote_original": "Have faith in this unseen claim until the conviction is born within you that it is so.", "primary_topic": "FAITH_PRAYER", "secondary_topics": ["ASSUMPTION", "PERSISTENCE"], "tags": ["faith", "conviction", "unseen"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-018", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 80, "quote_original": "Do not condition your desire. Just accept it as it comes to you. Give thanks for it to the point that you are grateful for having already received it – then go about your way in peace.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["ASSUMPTION", "FEELING", "FAITH_PRAYER"], "tags": ["desire", "gratitude", "acceptance", "peace"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-019", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 93, "quote_original": "If you would catch that which is beyond your present capacity you must launch out into deeper waters, for, within your present consciousness such fish or desires cannot swim.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "secondary_topics": ["DESIRE", "SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["deeper-waters", "capacity", "desire", "transformation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "AYC-CUR-020", "corpus_id": "B001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "At Your Command", "source_year": 1939, "source_slug": "at_your_command", "source_paragraph": 108, "quote_original": "Recognition is the power that conjures in the world. Every state that you have ever recognized, you have embodied. That which you are recognizing as true of yourself today is that which you are experiencing.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM", "REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"], "tags": ["recognition", "state", "embodiment", "self-concept"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_at_your_command.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
